<title>USA: Cyclone Daniella leaves Mauritius, weakens.</title>
<headline>Cyclone Daniella leaves Mauritius, weakens.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tropical Cyclone Daniella is now moving away from Mauritius into the South Indian Ocean, private forecaster Weather Services Corp. said.</p>
<p>Heavy rains and damaging winds have subsided in Mauritius. Top winds have decreased to 75 mph in the storm and it is now moving southeastward into open waters in the South Indian Ocean, threatening only shipping.</p>
<p>Daniella will continue to weaken.</p>
</text>
